## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design registry-driven per-tenant masking, consistent lineage, and CI across tenants, while handling late data and schema drift.

## Key Concepts

- Macro-based per-tenant masking
- Dynamic per-tenant schemas from a registry
- Schema drift guards and late data handling
- Global lineage tracking and cross-tenant isolation in CI

## Code Example

```javascript
// simplified macro skeleton
{% macro mask_for_tenant(field, tenant) -%}
  {% if tenant in var('full_access_tenants') -%}
    {{ field }}
  {% else -%}
    sha256({{ field }})
  {% endif -%}
{%- endmacro %}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test masking correctness across tenants in CI?
- How would you handle a tenant revocation of access mid-cycle?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design privacy-aware, tenant-scoped analytics with late-arriving data. Emphasizes incremental logic, governance, and lineage.

## Key Concepts
- Incremental models with composite keys (tenant_id, date, event_type)
- Field-level redaction controlled by privacy_flag via a macro
- Late-arriving data handled through a short lookback MERGE
- Schema drift guards using sources, tests, and snapshots
- Exposures to reflect lineage in dashboards

## Code Example
```sql
-- macros/redact_email.sql
{% macro redact_email(email, privacy_flag) -%}
  {% if privacy_flag -%}
    {{ return('REDACTED') }}
  {% else -%}
    {{ return(email) }}
  {% endif -%}
{% endmacro %}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the redact_email macro across combinations of privacy_flag and null emails?
- How would you scale this approach to thousands of tenants with varying data freshness SLAs?
